.TH TPAD 1 "17 July 2026" "" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
tpad \- simple, fast, and easy to use text editor.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tpad
.RI [ FILE ... ]
.br

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBtpad\fP is a text editor for plain text and source files. It provides a
GTK frontend on Linux (GTK 4 on current systems or GTK 3 for compatibility)
and a Qt 6 frontend on macOS, Windows, and Linux.
.PP
Use \fBFile \(-> Print...\fP or press \fBCtrl+P\fP to open the frontend's
system print dialog. The dialog provides the printers, print-to-file
destination, paper size, orientation, page range, and other options supplied
by the desktop print service.
.PP
Successful opens and saves move a file to the top of
\fBFile \(-> Open Recent\fP. Recording is enabled by default. Preferences can
disable it or set a maximum from 0 to 1,000,000 entries; the default is 100
and 0 means unlimited. Disabling history stops updates and disables Open
Recent without deleting the existing list.
.PP
Frequency Analysis examines the current selection, or the whole document when
nothing is selected, and displays a scrollable Unicode table with Character,
Code point, Count, and Percent columns.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Open the system print dialog for the current document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open the Preferences window.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit tpad.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Reverse the current text.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+Z
Redo the most recently undone edit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tpad.cfg
Per-user configuration data for the GTK frontend.
.TP
.I ~/.tpad.recent
Private, newest-first recent-file list shared by both frontends.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TPAD_RECENT_FILE
An absolute path that replaces \fI~/.tpad.recent\fP. Relative values are
ignored. This override is intended for isolated testing.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lp (1)
